---
import "../styles/custom.css"
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro"
const title = 'Pricing — Vectis Mail'
const description = 'Vectis Mail pricing — free Starter tier (3 domains, 25 mailboxes), Pro at $39 USD per tenant/month with unlimited domains, OIDC SSO, and priority support.'
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<title>{title}</title>
	<meta name="description" content={description} />
	<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
	<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
	<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
	<meta property="og:url" content="https://vectismail.com/pricing/" />
	<meta property="og:image" content="https://vectismail.com/og/default.png" />
	<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
	<meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
	<meta property="og:image:alt" content="Vectis Mail pricing — free Starter, $39 USD/tenant/month Pro" />
	<meta property="og:site_name" content="Vectis Mail" />
	<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
	<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
	<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
	<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://vectismail.com/og/default.png" />
	<meta name="theme-color" content="#0C0C0D" />
	<link rel="canonical" href="https://vectismail.com/pricing/" />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />
	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "SoftwareApplication",
		"name": "Vectis Mail",
		"applicationCategory": "CommunicationApplication",
		"applicationSubCategory": "Email Server",
		"operatingSystem": "Linux",
		"description": description,
		"url": "https://vectismail.com/pricing/",
		"softwareVersion": "0.1.19",
		"publisher": {
			"@type": "Organization",
			"name": "Veltara Works",
			"url": "https://veltaraworks.com"
		},
		"offers": [
			{
				"@type": "Offer",
				"name": "Starter",
				"price": "0",
				"priceCurrency": "USD",
				"availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
				"description": "Free forever. Up to 3 domains, 25 mailboxes per domain, sending API, inbound webhooks, admin dashboard, Roundcube webmail, DKIM/SPF/DMARC, automatic TLS, backup and restore, RBAC + TOTP MFA, atomic updates, IP warmup, RBL monitoring, Prometheus-format metrics and health alerts (Grafana + Loki dashboards optional, off by default), community support.",
				"category": "free",
				"url": "https://vectismail.com/getting-started/installation"
			},
			{
				"@type": "Offer",
				"name": "Pro",
				"price": "39",
				"priceCurrency": "USD",
				"availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
				"description": "Per tenant per month, never per email — unlimited send volume. Everything in Starter plus unlimited domains, unlimited mailboxes per domain, per-domain analytics dashboard, per-domain spam controls (reject thresholds, greylisting, allow/block lists), OIDC SSO (Google, Azure AD, Keycloak), priority email support, and offline use through your current paid period (typically up to ~30 days on monthly plans) if ValidonX is temporarily unreachable. One subscription covers unlimited Vectis Mail installs operated by your organisation.",
				"category": "subscription",
				"priceSpecification": {
					"@type": "UnitPriceSpecification",
					"price": "39",
					"priceCurrency": "USD",
					"unitText": "per tenant per month",
					"billingIncrement": "1",
					"billingDuration": "P1M"
				},
				"url": "https://vectismail.com/upgrade/"
			}
		]
	})} />
	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "FAQPage",
		"mainEntity": [
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Why is Pro priced per tenant and not per email?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Because metered sending punishes growth. SendGrid, Postmark, Resend, and SES all price per email past a base bucket, so your email bill rises with your send volume. Vectis Mail never charges per email — Pro is a flat $39 USD per tenant per month for unlimited send volume, whether you send 10,000 or 10 million. A tenant is your organisation, and one subscription covers unlimited Vectis Mail installs you operate." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Do I need a license to use Vectis Mail?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The Starter tier is free forever with no license required. Pro is licensed through ValidonX." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "What happens if my license expires?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Your mail server keeps running and all core mail delivery continues. If a payment fails, Pro features keep working through a 21-day grace window while we retry; after that they revert to Starter limits, but your data is never locked." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Can I self-host without any external dependencies?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Starter works fully offline. Pro checks ValidonX for entitlements and keeps working offline through your current paid period if ValidonX is temporarily unreachable." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "What server do I need?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Minimum: 2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM, 40 GB SSD, Ubuntu 22.04+. Recommended for production: 4 vCPU, 8 GB RAM, 100 GB SSD. Any VPS provider works." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Can I resell Vectis Mail as a hosted service?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Vectis Mail is licensed under the Business Source License 1.1. You may run it for your own organisation and your own end users, including operating mail for customers of your organisation — but you may not offer Vectis Mail itself to third parties on a hosted, embedded, or managed-service basis in a way that competes with Veltara Works's paid version(s). For resale or hosted-platform licensing, contact licensing@veltaraworks.com." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "When does Vectis Mail become Apache 2.0?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Each version of Vectis Mail converts to Apache License 2.0 four years after that version's first public release — not a single repo-wide flip. For example, v0.1.0-beta1 (released 2026-04-25) converts on 2030-04-25; v0.1.12 (released 2026-05-10) converts on 2030-05-10. Source is available throughout, and once a version reaches its Change Date, anyone can fork, host, or relicense that specific version under Apache 2.0." }
			}
		]
	})} />
</head>
<body class="marketing-page">
	<nav class="marketing-nav">
		<a href="/" class="logo"><img src="/brand/logos/vectis-mail-logo-white.webp" alt="Vectis Mail" width="181" height="34" /></a>
		<div>
			<a href="/features/">Features</a>
			<a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a>
			<a href="/alternatives/">Compare</a>
			<a href="/getting-started/">Docs</a>
			<a href="/notes/">Notes</a>
			<a href="/about/">About</a>
			<a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
		</div>
	</nav>

	<main>

	<section class="section" style="text-align: center;">
		<h1>Vectis Mail&trade; pricing</h1>
		<p class="subtitle">Self-hosted email — never priced per send. Free Starter tier, $39 USD/tenant/month Pro for unlimited volume. Start free, upgrade when you need more.</p>

		<div class="pricing-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(280px, 380px)); justify-content: center;">
			<div class="pricing-card">
				<div class="tier">Starter</div>
				<div class="price">Free</div>
				<div class="period">forever</div>
				<ul>
					<li>Up to 3 domains</li>
					<li>Up to 25 mailboxes per domain</li>
					<li>Admin dashboard</li>
					<li>Webmail (Roundcube)</li>
					<li>Sending API + batch sending</li>
					<li>Inbound webhooks (full body)</li>
					<li>Sieve filter management</li>
					<li>DKIM/SPF/DMARC</li>
					<li>Automatic TLS</li>
					<li>Built-in metrics &amp; health alerts (Grafana + Loki optional)</li>
					<li>IP warmup &amp; RBL monitoring</li>
					<li>Backup &amp; restore</li>
					<li>Community support</li>
				</ul>
				<a href="/getting-started/installation/" class="btn-primary" style="display: block; text-align: center;">Get Started</a>
			</div>

			<div class="pricing-card featured">
				<div class="tier">Pro</div>
				<div class="price">$39</div>
				<div class="period">USD per tenant / month</div>
				<ul>
					<li>One subscription, unlimited Vectis installs</li>
					<li>Everything in Starter, plus:</li>
					<li>Unlimited send volume &mdash; never priced per email</li>
					<li>Unlimited domains</li>
					<li>Unlimited mailboxes per domain</li>
					<li>Per-domain analytics dashboard</li>
					<li>Per-domain spam controls &mdash; thresholds, greylisting, allow/block lists</li>
					<li>OIDC SSO</li>
					<li>Priority email support</li>
				</ul>
				<a href="/upgrade/" class="btn-primary" style="display: block; text-align: center;">Buy Pro — $39 USD/mo</a>
				<p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.5; opacity: 0.85;">At ~1M emails/month, SendGrid Pro runs ~$89.95+ plus $30/mo per dedicated IP, and Resend Scale climbs from $90 toward $1,150. Vectis Pro is <strong>$39 flat</strong> &mdash; same price whether you send 10,000 or 10 million.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<p class="subtitle" style="margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">
			Running mail for client domains, or need SAML, an SLA, or
			compliance/DSAR support? Agency and Enterprise plans are in the works
			&mdash; <a href="/talk-to-us/">tell us what you need</a> and we'll size it
			with you.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Starter vs Pro at a glance</h2>
		<div class="compare-table-wrap" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
			<table class="compare-table">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Feature</th>
						<th scope="col">Starter</th>
						<th scope="col">Pro</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr><td>Price</td><td>Free forever</td><td>$39 USD / tenant / month</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Domains</td><td>Up to 3</td><td>Unlimited</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Mailboxes per domain</td><td>Up to 25</td><td>Unlimited</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Sending API + batch sending</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Inbound webhooks (full body)</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Admin dashboard</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Webmail (Roundcube)</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Sieve filter management</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>DKIM / SPF / DMARC</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Automatic TLS</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Monitoring (metrics + health alerts; Grafana + Loki optional)</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>IP warmup &amp; RBL monitoring</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Backup &amp; restore</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Per-domain analytics dashboard</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Per-domain spam controls (thresholds, greylisting, allow/block)</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>OIDC SSO (Google, Azure AD, Keycloak)</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Support</td><td>Community</td><td>Priority email</td></tr>
					<tr><td>Offline use if ValidonX is unreachable</td><td>n/a</td><td>Through current paid period</td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
		<div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(400px, 1fr));">
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Why per tenant and not per email?</h3>
				<p>Because metered sending punishes growth. SendGrid, Postmark, Resend, and SES all price per email past a base bucket, so your bill rises with your send volume. Vectis Mail <strong>never charges per email</strong> — Pro is a flat $39 USD per tenant per month for unlimited volume, the same price whether you send 10,000 or 10 million. A tenant is your organisation, and one subscription covers unlimited Vectis Mail installs you operate.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Do I need a license to use Vectis Mail?</h3>
				<p>The Starter tier is free forever with no license required. Pro is licensed through <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">ValidonX</a>, our licensing and billing platform.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>What happens if my Pro license expires?</h3>
				<p>Your mail server keeps running and all core mail delivery (Postfix, Dovecot) continues working. If a payment fails, Pro features keep working through a 21-day grace window while we retry; after that, Pro features (analytics, advanced spam controls, OIDC SSO, unlimited domains and mailboxes) revert to Starter limits but your data is never locked.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Can I self-host without any external dependencies?</h3>
				<p>Yes. The Starter tier works fully offline. Pro checks <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">ValidonX</a> for entitlements and keeps working offline through your current paid period if ValidonX is temporarily unreachable, with entitlements cached in Postgres.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>What server do I need?</h3>
				<p>Minimum: 2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM, 40 GB SSD, Ubuntu 22.04+. Recommended for production: 4 vCPU, 8 GB RAM, 100 GB SSD. Any VPS provider works.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Can I resell Vectis Mail as a hosted service?</h3>
				<p>No. Vectis Mail is licensed under the <a href="https://github.com/Veltara-Works/vectis/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">Business Source License 1.1</a>. You may run it for your own organisation and your own end users — including operating mail for customers of your organisation. You may <strong>not</strong> offer Vectis Mail itself to third parties on a hosted, embedded, or managed-service basis in a way that competes with Veltara Works's paid version(s). For resale or hosted-platform licensing arrangements, contact <a href="mailto:licensing@veltaraworks.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">licensing@veltaraworks.com</a>.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>When does Vectis Mail become Apache 2.0?</h3>
				<p>Each <em>version</em> of Vectis Mail converts to Apache License 2.0 four years after that version's first public release — not a single repo-wide flip. For example, <code>v0.1.0-beta1</code> (released 2026-04-25) converts on 2030-04-25; <code>v0.1.12</code> (released 2026-05-10) converts on 2030-05-10. Source is available throughout, and once a version reaches its Change Date, anyone can fork, host, or relicense that specific version under Apache 2.0.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<p class="page-meta">Last updated <time datetime="2026-06-08">8 June 2026</time></p>

	</main>

	<SiteFooter />
</body>
</html>
